# AI Recipe Parser Feature

Paste a recipe URL → AI extracts all details → Review and save.

## Architecture

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[User pastes URL] --> B[Frontend calls Edge Function]
    B --> C[Edge Function fetches page HTML]
    C --> D[Gemini parses recipe content]
    D --> E[Return structured JSON]
    E --> F[Frontend shows review form]
    F --> G[User saves recipe to DB]
```

## Proposed Changes

### Backend

#### [NEW] Supabase Edge Function: `parse-recipe`
- **Input:** `{ url: string }`
- **Process:**
  1. Fetch HTML from URL (handle CORS)
  2. Extract text content (strip scripts/styles)
  3. Send to Gemini with structured prompt
  4. Parse response into recipe schema
- **Output:**
```json
{
  "name": "Green Goddess Pasta",
  "servings": 4,
  "total_time_mins": 30,
  "web_source": "https://...",
  "instructions": "Step 1...",
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Pasta", "quantity": 400, "unit": "g", "category": "Pantry" }
  ]
}
```

---

### Frontend

#### [NEW] `QuickAddPage.tsx`
- URL input field with "Parse" button
- Loading state while AI processes
- Review form pre-filled with extracted data
- Edit capability before saving
- "Save Recipe" button

#### [MODIFY] [App.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mheyi/HeyinkMeals/src/App.tsx)
- Add route `/recipes/quick-add`

